# Environment this repository reads. Copy to .env, which is gitignored.
#
# Nothing in the tree loads this file. There is no dotenv dependency and no
# Makefile target that sources it — `.env` is a convention for whoever is
# running the stack, and the process reads the environment it was given. So
# `export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)`, or a shell that does it for you.

# Google AI Studio key for the model-backed IntentInterpreter.
#
# Read by cmd/agent, and only when it is started with `-interpreter gemini`.
# The default is `-interpreter scripted`, which needs no key and no network:
# `make demo` has to come up without either, and the golden numbers every
# screenshot in this repository shows are the scripted five prompts.
#
# There is no fallback. `-interpreter gemini` with this unset refuses to start
# rather than quietly using the scripted table — an agent asked for a model and
# handed a fixed table produces a screenshot nobody can attribute.
#
# One caution about the free tier, measured rather than assumed: the pinned
# model aliases (gemini-2.0-flash and friends) answer 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED
# with `limit: 0` on every quota, which is *no allocation* rather than *used
# up*. The rolling aliases answer. That is why -gemini-model defaults to
# gemini-flash-latest.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
